{
  "_comment": "Mechanism table of the setup engine (recommendation overhaul D3, author 2026-10-22): one row per (lever group, symptoms, phases, speed classes, direction, anchor). Symptoms: US = front axle limiting, OS = rear axle limiting, INST = open-loop unstable yaw. INST uses the OS direction of a row unless a row names INST for that lever and phase (rear saturation = stability loss, Hoffman 2008). Left / right levers always change together (SEG p. 263). Directions are words; the sign comes from the registry direction_semantics (setup_parameters.json), never from this file (damper clicks: increasing = softer).",
  "_comment_anchors": {
    "MM": "Milliken & Milliken 1995, Race Car Vehicle Dynamics (bib key to verify)",
    "SEG": "Segers 2014, Analysis Techniques for Racecar Data Acquisition (bib key to verify)",
    "TE": "Trzesniowski & Eder 2019, Handbuch Rennwagentechnik Bd. 5 (bib Trzesniowski.2019)",
    "KATZ": "Katz, Race Car Aerodynamics (bib key: Katz, edition to verify)"
  },
  "phase_groups": {
    "BRK": [
      "entry_1_brake"
    ],
    "TIN": [
      "entry_2_turnin"
    ],
    "APX": [
      "apex_3"
    ],
    "EXIT": [
      "exit_4",
      "exit_5"
    ]
  },
  "mechanism_names": {
    "M1": "roll stiffness distribution",
    "M2": "transient load transfer (low-speed dampers)",
    "M4": "aero balance",
    "M5": "tyre working point",
    "M6": "drivetrain",
    "M7": "brake balance"
  },
  "_comment_not_levers": "Out of scope, deliberately not levers: high-speed dampers, blow-off, arb_front_mount (ruling D3). [2026-10-23, 4f item 1: ride heights removed from this list -- M4 levers at high speed, valid outside the ground-effect stall regime.]",
  "_comment_m2_phases": "M2 acts on transient load transfer only: never APX (TE p. 254; SEG pp. 259-263).",
  "_comment_side_effect": "side_effect.text from TE Tab. 5.14 pp. 296-297 (wording ruled by the author 2026-10-22, 4e item 7), set on the rows whose direction the table entry describes: camber more negative, toe_front more toe-out, diff_position increase. Rows in the opposite direction keep text null (no wording ruled); the source stays named so the slot is traceable.",
