  "_comment_engineer_preference": "Engineer preference weight (D3): the elicited cells of the retired recommendations.json matrix (moved 2026-10-22, provenance kept). Per (symptom, phase, speed class) a candidate gets preference 1 when the cell names its lever with the table's direction (cell_directions mapped through the registry direction_semantics), else 0 (4e item 6, 2026-10-22). Preference only orders candidates, never adds a lever, never sets a direction.",
  "_comment_engineer_unsupported": {
    "_comment": "engineer cells not supported by the literature table (author ruling 2026-10-22, 4e item 6): a cell whose direction contradicts the table, or that names a lever the table has no row for at that symptom / phase / speed class, is ignored -- it gives no preference to any candidate. Computed by setup_engine.unsupported_preference_cells; tests/test_setup_engine.py checks this list against it. [2026-10-23, 4f: US-BRK-high left this list -- its ride-height entries (front decrease, rear increase) now match M4 at high speed; its wing_position increase still contradicts M4-wing-US and gives no preference. It is the one cell that mixes supported and unsupported levers; the check is per lever.]",
    "US-BRK-low": "toe_front more toe-out: the table has toe_front only at turn-in (TIN, low speed), not under braking",
    "OS-APX-high": "camber_fl / camber_fr less negative: the table has no front-camber row for OS",
    "INST-BRK-med": "ride_height_front increase / ride_height_rear decrease: ride heights are M4 levers at high speed only (4f), the cell is medium speed",
    "INST-BRK-high": "toe_front more toe-out under braking: no toe_front row under braking, and more toe-out is the US direction (M5-toe-front-US), opposite to the OS / INST one"
  },
